 ;; Taken from Tolkien Gateway
 {:entry/name       "Rings of Power"
  :entry/type       :entry.type/thing
  :entry/description "The Rings of Power were magic rings created by the _Elves_ of _Eregion_. Nineteen Great rings were made with the knowledge obtained from _Sauron_, guised as _Annatar_, with him aiding in the creation of most. _Sauron_ alone forged the twentieth Great Ring, called _The One Ring_ or the Ruling Ring, secretly in the fires of _Mount Doom_."
  :entry/page       [275 276 288 289]
  :entry/appears-in [[:chapter/name "Of the Rings of Power and the Third Age"]]}

 ;; Taken from Tolkien Gateway
 {:entry/name       "The One Ring"
  :entry/type       :entry.type/thing
  :entry/description "The One Ring was an ancient artifact created by the Dark Lord _Sauron_ in the _Second Age_ for the purpose of ruling over the Free peoples of _Middle-earth_, mainly the _Elves_."
  :entry/page       [255 268 275 276 277 280 282 283 286 290 291]
  :entry/appears-in [[:chapter/name "Akallabêth"]
                     [:chapter/name "Of the Rings of Power and the Third Age"]]}

 ;; Taken from Tolkien Gateway
 {:entry/name       "Three Rings of the Elves"
  :entry/type       :entry.type/thing
  :entry/description "The Three Rings were magical artifacts, three of the _Rings of Power_. They were forged by _Celebrimbor_ and granted the power to preserve the beauty of things by stopping change and warding off the decay of time and postponing the weariness of the world. They had the greatest power of the _Rings of Power_. The Three Rings were named _Vilya_, _Narya_, and _Nenya_ after the principal elements of air, fire, and water (respectively)."
  :entry/page       [275 276 286 292]
  :entry/appears-in [[:chapter/name "Of the Rings of Power and the Third Age"]]}

 ;; Taken from Tolkien Gateway
 {:entry/name       "Seven Rings of the Dwarves"
  :entry/type       :entry.type/thing
  :entry/description "The Seven Dwarf-rings were the _Rings of Power_ given to seven Dwarf Lords by _Sauron_ in the guise of _Annatar_.\n\nApparently the Lords were the Kings of the Seven Houses, as _Gandalf_ mentions that the Rings were given to the \"Dwarf-kings\"."
  :entry/page       [276 277 286 289]
  :entry/appears-in [[:chapter/name "Of the Rings of Power and the Third Age"]]}

 ;; Taken from Tolkien Gateway
 {:entry/name       "Nine Rings of Men"
  :entry/type       :entry.type/thing
  :entry/description "The Nine Rings were the _Rings of Power_ that _Sauron_ used to corrupt _Men_ to his service. Those who took the Nine Rings became the _Nazgûl_.\n\nThe Nine Rings were made along with the other _Rings of Power_ in _Eregion_ and were forged by Elven smiths under the guidance of _Sauron_. They were kept in the House of the Mírdain, but all rings save the Three Elven rings were captured by _Sauron_ when he attacked _Eregion_. He gave nine of them to _Men_, and it was said that three of those that received them were _Númenórean_ lords, and another was from the East."
  :entry/page       [255 277 286 289]
  :entry/appears-in [[:chapter/name "Akallabêth"]
                     [:chapter/name "Of the Rings of Power and the Third Age"]]}

